Session 27 final scorecard, all evidence-backed:

1. **D-DIRENT-PUBLISH-STALE-BASE-P195-360 (major) — FIXED AND VERIFIED** on 0.11.361. Implemented the full GPT-ruled Option-B contract (explicit validity bit, adopt-at-EX-acquire gate, stamp-after-install, release-time invalidation, creator-stamp subordination, per-reason counters), plus six missing-braces bugs the compiler confirmed across five files. Verified by the defect's own protocol: boards green at 32 and 8 nodes, 24 board-aged dirent_publish loops (historical rate predicted ~3 hits, observed 0), 60-round mkdir storm clean, exactly one gate arm all day — a backward-epoch slot-reclamation reset, the precise case the ruled `!=` compare exists for — and no pace regression.

2. **D-CACHE-COHERENCY-UV-COUNT-MISS-2332 (critical) — DISPROVED.** A degraded member (mount detached after pre-assert, before the body) reproduces rank1's incident signature exactly — `uv exp=128 got=124`, the missing 4 files being the sick member's own never-durable creates — while 23 cache_coherency and 11 zero_silent_loss runs on a healthy fleet were all green the same day. The Aug-1 incident had a documented sick member (test32, root disk full).

3. **New critical found, contained, and on the books: D-RSYNC-RENAME-DIRTY-CANCEL-MASS-SHUTDOWN-361.** Seventeen of 32 nodes independently hit a dirty `xfs_trans_cancel` in `xfs_rename` under rsync_paired — the known stale-base dirent-erasure family escaping through the pre-dirty revalidate's non-exchange-target gap. GPT-ruled containment shipped as 0.11.362: full target-expectation preflight returning -ESTALE (the kernel's own `retry_estale` re-walks and retries, so a vanished target degrades to a successful rename, not a shutdown), a dirty-cancel forensic probe with image cookies, and a stamp-timing micro-revert lever for the amplifier A/B. Five clean laps since, zero probe firings; the defect stays open for the producer hunt, and any recurrence now self-diagnoses.

Also hardened: run.sh now captures a kill-time kmsg phase census on any NO_TERMINAL failure (node stdout tails are lost to ssh buffering — that's why both prior events looked "silent"), and the hostload confounder (external game-server bursts to load 55) cost one excluded lap and is re-documented.

The rig is clean: 32/caw on 0.11.362, all mounted, marker current, ship-config knobs. Next in queue for the relay: continue rsync laps opportunistically at hostload <30, then the remaining criticals — write-unit authority via ICLUSTER (GPT's ranked item 1), certified foreign replay, and the TCP rig wiring that unblocks the open-unlink fix.

